  ('zcrm_1579374000139894024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000134092002', 'Karen Thompson', NULL, '05.28.2024 I spoke today with Seleste and she followed up about Karen''s enrollment, where she will be removed by Planstin''s IT dept from their MEC, where she will only have Zion for health-sharing and RCI for MEC. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-28 09:36:34', '2024-05-28 09:36:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139905003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026023246', 'Kristy Barber', NULL, '5-28-24 Kristy Barber called bc she''s being told to get  a diagnostic colonoscopy at age 43 for some stuff that''s going on with her right now. There''s no family history of anything. Apex/RCI already told her they won''t pay for it. I just read her the current Select+ Sharing Guidelines re colonoscopies. She will need to pay her $500 IUA first and submit the itemized bills for reimbursement. She understands and will follow the process.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-28 09:35:31', '2024-05-28 09:35:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139894019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117970009', 'Marissa O''Neal', NULL, '05.28.2024 Returning Seleste''s VM regarding Marissa''s lapse in coverage/insurance, given the RESTART eff 7/1/2024. Seleste was confused, but the lapse is due to the member, and not an technical glitch. I called Planstin today to chat with Seleste, Karen answered and transferred me to her. I confirmed that it was the member''s choice to change enrollment to 7/1 vs. 6/1. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-28 09:34:09', '2024-05-28 09:37:51'),
