  ('zcrm_1579374000139894008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077181001', 'Andrea McDonough', NULL, '0528.2024 Andrea called b/c her baby is breached, so midwife is no longer going to perform her services. They are in NY state, and the midwife there will not do home visits, only options in NY are C sections for breached babies. Midwife performed 37 visits of services, and 38 and on do not have a service provider for more pre-natal or post-natal.
Midwife needs to return some money back to Zion, given she is no longer performing the rest of the services with Andrea. The new midwife/doola is not medically licensed. Andrea is not willing to go into surgery.
Kevin at Zion, recommended the following:
1- Speak to the processor for the sharing request, April to discuss the options.
2- Give the medical advocacy team a chance to see what options of licensed midwives they have. 
Kevin did transfer us to April''s VM, Andrea left a message and we hung up.
I did learn from Andrea that the midwife''s license is not at stake should she perform her full services with a breached baby, it was a mere preference/fear. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-28 09:03:52', '2024-05-28 09:26:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139873011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000139791002', 'Maryjean Starr', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA Care +', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-05-28 09:02:46', '2024-05-28 09:02:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139894003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077566026', 'MaiLan Boris', NULL, '05.28.2024 Mailan called to learn if the new patient visit to her physical annual visit is included in the coverage with Planstin/MEC. I explained that part unfortunately is not covered by the MEC plan, and that sometimes providers add that to the appointment, and see if could ask them to do that. she was adamant they would not, given that she is a seasoned patient with them and they still want to apply that rule on her wellness chart.
She asked about colonoscopies, and I explained as long as all elements performing the service are in network for Planstin/PHCS, it is covered. Should they pull polyps they MIGHT turn it diagnostic, in turn becomes shareable with Zion, with the patient fulfilling the IUA only.
Mailan said that Jane Kassel had shared with her that the 1ST COLONOSCOPY on the plan is covered 100% no matter whether they pull polyps or not, and after that it will be coded according to what surfaces in the screening. I had not heard of that, and told her that I would do a little investigation and call her back. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-28 08:53:39', '2024-05-28 08:53:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139884003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130291039', 'Erica Henderson', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on vm. Sent email to reschedule welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2024-05-28 08:02:15', '2024-05-28 08:02:15'),
