  ('zcrm_1579374000139626019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000139729018', 'Raeanna Clarke', NULL, '5-22-24 Raeanna is 29 and turning 30 in Dec. 2024. Came to me via Andrea Hinman. She tried signing up for medical on C4. Then she chose dental which she says wiped away her medical from her account. However, her account doesn''t show any enrollment ever for medical. She doesn''t actually have a SEP, so she doesn''t qualify for C4 anyhow. She does have Delta Dental successfully. We are looking at CARE+. She has food allergies and had to change diet. She needs to see a dietitian and start a food journal. She was paying $190 before it ended around Dec. 31st. For some reason her former broker won''t return her calls or help her anymore. Nobody ever responded with C4 either. CARE+ is the cheapest and possibly choose the $2500 IUA for $185 monthly until she turns 30 in Dec. Then it moves to $205 in Dec.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-22 21:19:30', '2024-05-22 21:19:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139626014', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000139748167', 'Maryjean Starr', NULL, '5-22-24 Maryjean just learned that Cobra ended on May 17th. She was then declined a private insurance option bc of a concussion from 2017. I sent her instructions to set up a C4 account. She needs a June 1st start date. We might be able to move her to MCS or America''s Choice for July onward if she wants. We will look it over on Friday morning.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-22 21:10:49', '2024-05-22 21:10:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139626003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025756253', 'Robin Beck', NULL, '5-22-24 Robin is enrolling in HAB now, EC $200 for July 1st. She completed the Change Form to remove Apex MEC as well for July 1st. She is now clear on losing HSA compliance moving forward. She already used all of her HSA funds for issues earlier in 2024. She was paying $596. Now for July 1st, she will pay $474.65 + $25 EC / $1500 IUA = $499.65 on 20th of the month +$200 on the 1st = $699.65.  She will wait to do her daughters wellness visit in July to avoid network limitations. She''s thrilled about the mental health aspect for her kids as well. That outweighs the loss of HSA tax savings.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-22 16:34:31', '2024-05-22 16:49:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139617003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122117002', 'Leisa Heuple', NULL, '05.22.2024 Leisa called to learn what steps she needs to take in attempt to get shared for her dermatology appointment. Dermatology - precancerous mole removed - lab costs - follow up to read lab results - possible additional scrapping/cutting around the area in the future. Zion sharing request. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-22 16:21:28', '2024-05-22 16:37:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139600072', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114224002', 'Federico Gaytan Jr', NULL, '05.22.2024 Frederico called to unfortunately request if he can put a pause on billing/pausing the membership. I shared that based on my past experience with a few other members requesting the same thing, I''ve learned they cannot pause the membership, but to speak to his advisor for options that would offer him less premium per month. We were not sure if Leonardo Moraes was still active, even if it did say in the pop up for his information. I offered him a call back tomorrow after learning who is advisor it, so he can start there. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-22 15:58:04', '2024-05-22 16:47:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139600062', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061522092', 'Nancy Allawos', NULL, '05.22.2024 Nancy called to confirm there isn''t anything she needs to do to be ready for when she turns 65 YO. I went over what I see Patti do and that''s the minimal of sending an email 2 months prior to the birthday. I transferred her to Patti''s VM and sent her an email to review us. She is extremely satisfied with how the company is run, the service from MPB and the benefits put together in her membership. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-22 15:16:42', '2024-05-22 15:16:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139598154', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082048002', 'Maginel Galt', NULL, '5/22/24: Maginel called trying to get into member portal, but didn''t have her ID number. I provided her with the ID number. She wanted to change her address so I navigated her to the form and assisted her with getting it submitted properly. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-05-22 14:21:29', '2024-05-22 14:21:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139570104', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130526365', 'Isaiah Burdon', NULL, '5-22-24  I spoke with Halie at Five Rings per the best path forward since today is the deadline to communicate with NLG about the late payment.  The following is what Halie shared as best practices and repercussions.

 I sent this to Isaiah, per his policy. 

"There''s an issue with the payment for your life insurance policy with National Life Group.

It appears that your account is set for auto draft on the 10th of the month.  Assuming your April 10th payment processed successfully, you have 70 days from the last payment made to make your next payment. You will have to make payments for the missed payment/s and then again on the next draft date. Does that make sense?  Basically, you have to make up for the missed payment and get back on track with the current payment due.

The best way to rectify this when you are ready and able is to call National Life Group at 1-800-732-8939. They are based in VT in EST."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-22 14:07:54', '2024-05-22 14:12:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139570099', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130526392', 'Brianna Krampetz', NULL, '5-22-24 Heard from Brianna via text and she asked for an extension or that the repercussions are for late payment. Her banking account was compromised and the account shows as having insufficient funds. My response to her was as follows after speaking with Halie at Five Rings:

"There''s an issue with the payment for your life insurance policy with National Life Group.

It appears that your account is set for auto draft on the 10th of the month.  Assuming your April 10th payment processed successfully, you have 70 days from the last payment made to make your next payment. You will have to make payments for the missed payment/s and then again on the next draft date. Does that make sense?  Basically, you have to make up for the missed payment and get back on track with the current payment due.

The best way to rectify this when you are ready and able is to call National Life Group at 1-800-732-8939. They are based in VT in EST."

I sent more clarification via another email.

"I want to offer a little more clarity about the possible repercussions for non-payment of your National Life Group term policy. If they don''t receive your payment within 70 days following the last successful payment, then your policy will lapse. Hopefully, that will give you enough time to sort out your bank account problems."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-22 14:07:11', '2024-05-22 14:17:20'),
