  ('zcrm_1579374000139598093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110552002', 'Sheryl Hadley', NULL, '5/22/24: 1. Called Sheryl. She has Hypernutremia (low sodium) and getting some lab work done. I explained that with her Planstin MEC, only a standard lipid panel is included and shared our discount lab resources with her via email. Ia also informed her that if the tests were part of a sharing request, then they could be shareable after her IUA is met. She''s going to call Zion to check and see if that condition is shareable. 
2. She had a mammogram done last week that she thinks it''s diagnostic even though it wasn''t performed in response to an issue. I informed her that in order for Planstin to pay, it needs to be coded preventive. 
