  ('zcrm_1579374000139111122', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045798106', 'richard rosin', NULL, '5-15-24 Rick called to finalize membership for all family members. Kyle is 26 and how now has a lapse in membership and will be living in CA. So, we had to abort mission on the Premium products with Sedera. We went to the Secure HSA with RCI MEC $309.20 (but showed as $306.20 upon enrollment which Vinnie has since fixed) to obtain compliance. Kyle is getting a skin thing removed for $900. Rick has already paid $500 towards  this issue. He now understands it will be pre-x. Even if we could have kept Kyle with Sedera, he already had a lapse in membership, so pre-x would have started over with Sedera as well.  I also waived the $100 enrollment fee since Kyle is already a member but just aging up at 26. 
Rick and his wife Bule had struggles with Redirect, so he stopped using them and didn''t know he could have cancelled them. So, he chose to remove Redirect for June 1st and added HAB for him and wife. Since they removed Redirect now the new SDHC $500 ES 50-59 is $777.65 and add HAB at $165 = $942.65. They are paying about $973 now. So, they can save a little money and have much better benefits and experience. He''s all set for that to begin June 1st. 
Final step is to help with his daughter''s membership. We plan to drop Planstin MEC and add HAB for June 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-15 12:36:52', '2024-05-15 16:17:11'),
