  ('zcrm_1579374000139073064', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000139074168', 'Alan Depew', NULL, '5-13-24 Alan is 63 and Christina Malley is 53 in June, 2024. Alan watched the video. He''s retired already and she is retiring on Sept. 5th. They need an Oct. 1st start date. He thought he wanted a UHC or Kaiser plan until he understood how comprehensive these memberships are. He had a kidney stone about 1 1/2 years ago. He''s on cholesterol meds and hasn''t been hospitalized. It''s well managed with meds. Alan looked at Covered CA and it would cost them about $2000 per month and in FL at least $500 per person. They travel domestically and internationally. They do their wellness visits, dental cleanings, vision screenings, gym memberships, colonoscopies and mammograms! They don''t have need for mental health. Super interested in Premium Care $1000/$575 and HAB $165 = $740 for Oct. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-13 23:02:38', '2024-05-13 23:02:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139073054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000139464012', 'Matthew Neumann', NULL, '5-13-24 Matt is 24, single, just left his job with insurance. He just started working with Justin Acker, who referred him to MPB. Matt is responsible for paying for his own healthcare now. He watched the video. He''s healthy, no pre-x in 36 months, no meds, no tobacco. His hasn''t done much of his wellness visits lately but is happy to do so, including his dental cleanings. He doesn''t need vision screening, nutritional health, mental health or gym membership. He has his own gym equipment in his house. So, HAB might not be worth the money for him. He''s very interested in Premium Care $237/$1000, but also wants the info for HAB to review. We are meeting again on Wed to enroll.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-13 21:14:54', '2024-05-17 14:26:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139073049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120746001', 'Jennifer Zrubek', NULL, '5-13-24 Jennifer called to find a new health insurance plan bc she''s confused by Zion. She was recently diagnosed with Hashimoto''s by a holistic practitioner. Her traditional MD told her she "might" have Hashimoto''s from her blood work but didn''t diagnose it. She went to a holistic Dr. who is helping to treat her. I explained alternative care must be pre-approved and her regular visits and labs will certainly count towards her $1000 IUA. I read through the questions for America''s Choice and Hashimoto''s might not be allowed via underwriting. She can''t join Kaiser now and she''s already paid close to $1000 toward her IUA. So, there''s no sense in starting over with a deductible.  I suggested she calls the MPB Concierge Team and asks for help in the entire process. She seems to feel better and will follow through with the process.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-13 20:28:09', '2024-05-13 20:28:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139073044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069411014', 'Rhyan Rosin', NULL, '5-13-24 Rhyan is Richard Rosin''s daughter who aged up. I might suggest she drops Planstin and replaces it with HAB. She can stay on Zion since she''s been a member since July 1st, 2021. Price is only $3 different if she moved to Premium Care with Sedera.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-13 20:26:27', '2024-05-13 20:26:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139073039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045798106', 'richard rosin', NULL, '5-13-24 Rick is open to my ideas for the best option for each family member. Rhyan, his daughter has SECURE HSA. We may want to move her to CARE+ and HAB since the PHCS network is terrible in Aspen. Kyle can join Premium Care $1000/$237 and possibly add HAB as well. Rick and his wife can drop Redirect and move to Premium Care $575/$1000 (up from $500) and add HAB for $165 = $740.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-13 20:24:17', '2024-05-15 12:28:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139064042', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045798106', 'richard rosin', NULL, '05.13.2024 He called and left a message regarding trying to get in touch with Wendy, to remove his son who''s turning 26 and open his own membership. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-13 17:46:44', '2024-05-13 17:46:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139073034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045798106', 'richard rosin', NULL, '5-13-24 Left vm to help Ricki with his 26 year old son with a new membership. Premium Care may be best to start with.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-13 17:32:17', '2024-05-13 17:32:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139073026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000139074004', 'Pietro Simonetti', NULL, '5-13-24 Pietro enrolled his family. He included his daughter as a backup if there''s anything Medicaid won''t pay for. He''s keeping his dental and vision through Key Bank.  He got an auto renewal for his life insurance policy as well. So, I don''t need to run that illustration.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-13 17:24:26', '2024-05-13 17:25:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000139073018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000137607002', 'Amanda Caras', NULL, '5-13-24 Her life ins policy is issued for $200K at $33 per month for Standard Non-Tobacco.

