  ('zcrm_1579374000139064031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130351009', 'Kathleen Smith', NULL, '05.13.2024 Katie called to understand why she has received bills for a couple of preventive appointments: Bone density screening & mammogram. It turns out she had a lot of labwork done, and therefore was not covered and the mammogram facility has not billed Planstin yet.
I explained how to go about saving on the lab-work, given that now she understands it is an out of pocket expense. I guided her to:
1- Present as a cash pay patient on all the lab-work at LabCorp, except for the std lipid panel. Request to see if they have  cash pay discount to bring down the price from ~$900. If NO, then ask them if they would accept a receipt from purchasing those labs off of a discounted websites, to save money.
2- Call the mammogram facility and ask them to fax Planstin to bill them. If they are still clueless on how to proceed, I asked her to offer additional education by telling them that your preventive benefits are derived from the ACA guidelines on Healthcare.GOV, and all they have to is fax Planstin the bill so they can cover it.
One thing that I did not mention to Katie was that the $322.27 went towards her deductible. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-13 16:14:31', '2024-05-13 16:17:57'),
