  ('zcrm_1579374000138830056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000126854002', 'Rachel Johnson', NULL, '05.09.2024 Rachel called to learn how to proceed now that she has discovered she is pregnant. We talked about the Maternity Sharing Request and the surface details of the process. We talked about the IUA and 6 months deadline of each service. She was concerned that the maternity is 9 months, and I explained the details of the 6 month deadline. She asked if she can use a midwife, and I told her I know it is shareable, but I do not know if the midwife can be the end all be all for the entire maternity. I transferred her to Zion, and coached her on what to press and ask for. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-05-09 16:35:57', '2024-05-09 16:35:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000138861023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000143664002', 'Mary Ellen Francescani', NULL, '5-9-24 Mary Ellen is 53 and husband is 57, with 22 yr old daughter, another on state ins and the 3rd going to college and looking at their ins. Paolo Bonetti referred her to me and Nancy (she doens''t know her last name). Mary Ellen is a Nurse Practitioner and she opening her own small practice with one other person. She does integrative, functional medicine! She''s well aware of how the health ins world works. She''s opening her practice likely in a DPC model but she doesn''t need a DPC herself. BUT, her clients could use it and HAB w/DPC. I quoted her CARE+ and HAB. She''s not sure if they need HAB yet but might add it in a year or so. She''ll review it. Husband takes Lexipro and ADD med. Daughter is low in iron bc she''s a vegetarian and college runner. But, Mary Ellen thinks that might subside now that''s she done with college running. She gets iron infusions and knows that will be at their own cost if she still needs them. Otherwise, they are all healthy.  She''s looking to get started by Aug. 1st or Sept. 1st. I quoted her CARE+ $875/$1000 and HAB $250, plus $125/$25. She seems to know of Zion already... HAB with DPC could be an incredible option for her patients at her new clinic. She''s also thrilled to hear about Full Scripts. She has that for her clients already but really sees the value in it!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-09 16:28:10', '2024-05-09 16:34:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000138861018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521486', 'Ryan Ashley', NULL, '5-9-24 Ryan is paying $796.50 / $1000 EF, no MEC for MPB CareZ Worksite when turns 50. Premium Care with Sedera is $837, but includes mammo and colonoscopy. If any pre-x, they should stay put.  They have the lowest grandfathered price right now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-09 15:54:18', '2024-05-09 15:54:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000138861013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000006824147', 'Andrew Malishenko', NULL, '5-9-24 Andrew is certified with MPB and is working towards ins license still. He needed a little encouragement and boost to keep going. We had a great conversation. He will try to join a training or meet virtually with me the following week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-09 15:27:52', '2024-05-09 15:27:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000138829023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000137821002', 'Michael Ketchum', NULL, '5/9/24: Michael LVM saying we called, but there is no record. I clarified his start date with us and welcomed him aboard. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-05-09 14:36:38', '2024-05-09 14:36:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000138861008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011752368', 'Jill Fields', NULL, '5-9-24 Hi Wendy,

Yes, you can let Jill know that she is all set. I already informed her Needs Coordinator of the IUA change as well on her needs case.

Warm Regards,
Kristin

Sedera Member Services
855.973.3372
