  ('zcrm_1579374000138756008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144173420', 'Derek Lee', NULL, '5-8-24 Derek is looking at this for his group. He has 60% ownership with The Hope Institute and 100% ownership of Peri (?) Counseling. He also works at a university/medical school where he can get good group insurance for himself. He was diagnosed with Chrohn''s Disease last year and get $17K infusions. So, he''ll choose the school''s benefits for himself which he''s fine with. His group size is about 12. I shared CARE+ paired with HAB. His avg age is 30-45, so I quoted 30-49, $1000 IUA / $265 + HAB $107 = $372. Also, is $2500 IUA $250/$107 = $312. He can eliminate dental and vision with HAB. He hadn''t even thought of life ins yet. But, I explained value of post tax and reimbursement to employee instead of group life ins benefit. I also shared value of Living Benefits also. I will send CARE+ and HAB info to start.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-05-08 14:52:17', '2024-05-08 14:58:37'),
