  ('zcrm_1579374000138326134', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000093783010', 'Alyssa Beris', NULL, '5/2/24: Alyssa called to cancel her membership. She''s already reached out to her advisor and was sent instructions, but confused bc they were not clear. I guided her to the form on the website and let her know that if she filled it out today the cancellation would go into effect 6/1/24. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-05-02 14:25:57', '2024-05-02 14:25:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000138326129', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109671026', 'George Jarratt', NULL, '5/2/24: George called with questions regarding an open sharing request''s determination. 
His need was approved with the alternative therapy stipulations and care from Australia was denied sharing. 

When he bought the plan, he was under the impression that there were no caps and he could obtain treatment anywhere in the world. 
I shared that Zion makes decisions based on their guidelines, and in his case the cap is for the alternative treatment related to his need, but if he had other procedures that weren''t the glucose injections, then those wouldn''t fall under that cap. 
As for obtaining treatment outside of US, Zion does pay for injuries and acute care when you travel, but not choosing to have treatment outside of the US. And if he disagrees with their determination for the care he got while in Australia, then I suggest to file an appeal and provide documentations that proves it was actually acute care. 

He had questions about maternity sharing. I emailed a link to the maternity guidelines and answered questions he had regarding the types of services Zion shares and doesn''t share. 
AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-05-02 13:58:35', '2024-05-02 13:58:35'),
