3rd notice sent to member &amp; advisor via em 4/30', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-04-24 07:47:50', '2024-04-30 12:47:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000137764036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122131012', 'Qiuyi Lin Wright', NULL, '4-23-24 Qiuyi put in her resignation to The Hope Institute for April 30th. She''s getting benefits from her new employer. She completed the cancellation form and I also cc''ed Karina in a request to remove her from their List Bill. Qiuyi did not join the dental discount plan and she will keep her life ins plan. She''s all set on my end.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-04-23 16:56:39', '2024-04-23 16:56:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000137798063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124507139', 'Penny Dias', NULL, '04.23.2024 19081 Code - Breast biopsy. From preventive to diagnostic. I was not 100% on the CoPay plan regarding the transition from preventive to diagnostic, so I asked the couple if I can call them back to do a little research. They were patient and kind to accept that.
I video chatted with Joan on Teams, who pulled up the summary (not the plan details that the member usually gets from the company; Planstin or Zion), which said any out of patient surgery (which I believed a breast biopsy is), is not covered at all under preventive. BUT IT CERTAINLY should be once it transitions to diagnostic, which it did. I double checked with Kirk, another advisor and he concurred with me. 
I called Penny back, explained and asked if she would be okay with a 3-way call with ZION, to confirm the transition and if the process is parallel to a Secure plan that moves from preventative to diagnostic. Zion was closed, so the couple will call me tomorrow, upon the start of my shift, to attempt the 3-way call again. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-04-23 16:24:15', '2024-04-23 17:15:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000137798047', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000131740020', 'Duncan Burke', NULL, '04.23.2024 Called regarding a left knee issue. After numerous challenges in conversating with Duncan about his concern to get shared or not (did not share he had a sharing request already open, HAS NOT SCHEDULED HIS WELCOME CALL, did not share the reciprocation Zion attempted with him VIA the portal sharing request, all in while he was rude and impatient and unclear), I ended up coaching him on prefacing his conversation with "The HIPAA form was signed, it still says it''s pending, how do we proceed from here?". Then I transferred him to Zion, after I offered him their number.
RESENT him the scheduling link for the welcome call.
