The PHCS Network Results for a PCP & Nurse Practitioner near the zip code area 85258 .   NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-04-01 16:53:36', '2024-04-01 17:39:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136398013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032601365', 'Matt Holstein', NULL, '4-1-24 From Sedera per baby Kaia, "Hi Wendy,

Thank you for reaching out to Member Services. I show that the baby''s effective date on our end is 5.1.23.

Please let me know if you need any additional assistance.

Warm Regards,
Kristin"', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-04-01 15:45:11', '2024-04-01 15:45:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136398008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088254024', 'Juana Rincon Barrios', NULL, '4-1-24 Monthly payment in 2023 was $412.79 for all 12 months per her questioning.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-04-01 15:43:31', '2024-04-01 15:43:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136398003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000136382001', 'Eliza Volk', NULL, '4-1-24 Eliza is enrolling in HAB EO $107 for May 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-04-01 15:33:40', '2024-04-01 15:33:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000136393003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129213002', 'Monica Campbell', NULL, '04.01.2024 WWV Pap Smear with LabCorp - wanted to know if it is covered. I assured her it is, but to make sure the laboratory has her Planstin card, and she did that they do. She ended up paying for her appointment, b/c the provider''s office would not confirm that her bill will be covered, since they did not know who Planstin. We then did a 3-way with Planstin, Caitlyn answered and guided Monica through it all; submit a claim for reimbursement and to make sure to include: Name, Member#, Group#, A Detailed Estimate, Receipt and CPT code to make sure she gets reimbursed.
She wanted to know if her doctor is on the PHCS list; Dr. Chien Feng Gyno, but she was not. I explained that she can always present differently next time, through the RBP price model instead. Either way, she is covered.
Monica seemed fragile and overwhelmed with her plan and all the actions she feels responsible for, and worried she will say the wrong thing and not get covered. I assured her of all the legal elements on her side, and the concierge support to walk through it all, as well as the member empowerment that one does not have via traditional insurance. 
At the end of our call, Monica seemed in lighter spirits and has a stronger handle on how to maneuver the preventive appointments, at least.
Emailed Monica:
It was very nice to speak with you. I promised you directions to refer to at your leisure, to search the PHCS network on the Multiplan site.

Attached you will find:
The link to the ACA Guidelines on Healthcare.GOV
The link to the PHCS Network on Multiplan Link
One PowerPoint Slide to set up your search. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-04-01 15:27:37', '2024-04-01 17:43:43'),
