  ('zcrm_1579374000135525008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004762035', 'Traci Hoops', NULL, '3-19-24 Finally success with Traci''s colonoscopy that was deemed diagnostic since it was only 3 years past the most recent one where they removed polyps in the first visit, but none this time.  She was put through the ringer with Planstin and Zion saying they wouldn''t share in the cost. Planstin said no bc it wasn''t coded as wellness and Zion said No bc it was after the 6 months. She had been working on following Planstin''s instructions for recoding the entire time. Zion could see her communications with Planstin to prove her attempts and finally agreed to the appeal to share her cost above $1000 IAU. Yay!!

Hello Traci Hoops

We appreciate your membership and ongoing support of our Zion HealthShare community. It is our pleasure to inform you that our Appeals Committee has reviewed the request you submitted on for Traci Hoops - Diagnostic Colonoscopy/Colonic Polyps and have determined the request eligible for sharing.
The services we are able to share in are:

-Initial consultation with specialist

-Diagnostic colonoscopy on 07/11/23

-Pathology if needed


-Follow up visit with GI specialist 


Next Steps 
Now that your appeal request has been deemed eligible for sharing, the next important step is to proceed with the payment of your Initial Unshareable Amount (IUA), which is $1,000.Additionally, please ensure that you submit all relevant bills and itemized statements associated with your request through your member portal. To maintain eligibility for sharing, it is crucial that the IUA is paid in full, and bills submittedwithin six (6) months from the date of service. You may conveniently make IUA payments by directly paying your provider for eligible services or by reaching out to us at Zion HealthShare and making the payment over the phone. 
....', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-19 10:07:51', '2024-03-19 10:07:51'),
