  ('zcrm_1579374000135259124', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000131814002', 'Karyn Adams', NULL, '03.15.2024 Steven emailed me at 4:30pm requesting coupons and refills, I responded at 6:30 guiding him to fill out the form for specifics and  a successful research, and attaching the RX request form in the email.

"Thank you for reaching out.
I''d love to find you the savings for whichever script you have on hand. However, you will need your doctor to write you a refill if that''s what you need. Now, if you have more refills on the last script you filled out, then let me know which ones you''d like me to search by filling out the form attached here for your convenience.
https://www.cognitoforms.com/mpoweringbenefits1/prescriptionquoterequest

We are here at the concierge line M-F, 9am-8pm EST. Please do not hesitate to contact us for any guidance you may need."                     NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-03-15 17:35:54', '2024-03-15 17:35:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000135259104', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124806001', 'Brandon Harvey', NULL, '10/5 Christina called to better learn how to proceed with hernia issue with her son, and if a surgery is in order, what should she do. Appointment for newborn was pending - delayed billing letter denied called the on February. The ones from the appts 10/2 & 10/3 were sent just fine (received 10/9 & 10/10), but for some reason the one from 10/5 did not make it.
We did a 3-way called Planstin, Kaitlyn, asked for DOB, (Brenna=newborn daughter), $194 according to Planstin''s database, Doctor said it was pending, Planstin said in February that the bill was denied, they did not receive the provider''s bill till 2/20th. Christina had been in communication with the provider, when all the other bills around the same week were sent it with good timing. 
Kaitlyn, asked if they can prove they sent it in good time, Planstin would honor it. 
Some bills have been sent 10/10, 10/03 - claims fax#: 435-631-9478, email: claims@planstin.com. The pediatrics called Planstin in February 16th, about a claim, then they were advised that Planstin did not have that on file, which most likely prompted the to send it on the 20th.
Christina called the pediatrics while we were on the 3-way, Yolanda, and Kaitlyn requested the proof of when the 10/5 appt claim was sent. Yolanda was cooperative and searched the database to offer when it was sent.
IF the provider ended up sending that appt 10/5 too late, then it will need to be a write-off for the provider. 
Kaitlyn03/15 as a reference# for the conversation. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-03-15 16:56:16', '2024-03-15 17:18:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000135270056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000029000272', 'Katelyn Doty', NULL, '3-15-24 Katie is keeping the MEC. WWSRA, I believe is paying for MEC or HAS or both. She''s all set to go for April 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-15 15:36:02', '2024-03-15 15:36:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000135270051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000029000272', 'Katelyn Doty', NULL, '3-15-24 Hello Katelyn,

Your Health Access Benefit is made up of three key pieces that work together to provide you and your family with quality health care. These are your primary care, prescription, and preventive care.

Below you''ll find your personalized Digital Membership Packet, which includes all the information you need to get started using your Health Access Benefit.

Health Access Member ID: 522189940
Benefits Start Date: 04/01/2024

Primary Care
Status: Not enrolled.
When to Use: Your membership does not include any Direct Primary Care services.

Prescription
Status: Enrolled automatically!
When to Use: Use your prescription service anytime you need to fill a prescription from a pharmacy.


Preventive Care
