  ('zcrm_1579374000135057018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032016379', 'Maurine Killough', NULL, '3-12-24 Maurine is in CA and interested in HAS. But, she will need to keep MEC and add it in addition. It might not be worth the money for her. She''s been having a terrible time find a Dr. in the PHCS network. I sent her the link to try again. I can find over 200 Drs. within 20 miles that accept new patients. She knows to inquire directly with the Dr. in advance as well since she ran into that problem multiple times already. They said yes on the phone and no in person. She would use the annual physical, nutritional counseling, gym membership, dental cleaning and vision screening. Even with all of that, she might break even. It helps her know that she has choices. She had strep throat recently and needed a strep culture. She forgot about CirrusMD but she still would have to go to get the culture in person. She joined One Medical which gave her the virtual visit and the in-person visit for $80 and $150, I think she said. Now she remembers CirrusMD and will use that in the future, if need be. She''s also seeing a chiro for her hips being out of alignment. She might reach the $1000 IUA level. I read the Sharing Guidelines to her in relation to chiro. She might create a new Need in case it helps. I let her  know she may need a diagnosis and treatment plan from her chiro as well. She is 62 and doesn''t want to be forced to Medicare at age 65. She knows she can choose the HAS and use it once 65+. She can keep her HMA 2500 ongoing as well. She''s happy about that. She also mentioned a node on her thyroid but that Need never reached $1000. But, she was smart to create the Need in case it surpassed $1000. She''s going to review HAS and decide.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-12 12:43:15', '2024-03-12 12:43:15'),
