  ('zcrm_1579374000134948033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000131816011', 'Gloria Joy Sorensen', NULL, '3/11/24: Gloria called. She is still not able to submit a need with Zion. Her daughter had a choking incident 2/2/24 that resulted in an ER visit, and she needs to submit a need. 

I got Zion on the phone in an attempt to quickly resolve her status, and they transferred us to Planstin. Crystal said she is working on the integration files today. While on the phone, we checked on Gloria''s other employees Ryan Burke and Crystal Storey who were also not showing up in Zion and Crystal S. is not showing up at all with Planstin. While Gloria has been very patient through all this, she began to get frustrated over the phone and pushed that this needs to be resolved immediately. 

Crystal offered to work on this asap and advised me to also send her and email cc''ing her assistant manager Ember McDaniel about these files. 

I added Ryan B. and Crystal S. to Vinnie''s form and verified with Adan that Gloria is indeed on the spreadsheet, sent Planstin''s Crystal and Ember an email detailing the situation and requesting it be a high priority in order to restore member''s trust. Crystal said she would follow up, and I assured gloria i would follow up as well. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-03-11 12:08:14', '2024-03-11 12:09:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134944082', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000135465016', 'Todd Smith', NULL, '3-11-24 Aimee found me from the Naturally Inspired Podcast with Tammy and Jason Garcia. Aimee is turning 53 this year and her husband is 54. They live in Wellington, CO just north of FC. They did a Christian Healthshare Ministry a few years ago so they are familiar with it. They are both healthy and she''s a nutritionist, nurse and stays away from much of the traditional care. They prefer functional medicine and more natural solutions, hence her becoming a nutritionist. They do some preventative care and may need a colonoscopy soon, does some blood work, pap screening, etc. She loves the sounds of HAS as well. Her husband''s company will reimburse them up to about $1000 it sounds like and that''s close to chat they are paying now. So, CARE+ at $1000 IUA for $615 and HAS for $165 = $780. This is less than they are paying now and giving them many more benefits than what they have now.  She prefers chiropractic care, acupuncture, rolfing, functional medicine and mammogram every other year.  I let her know alternative care such as acupuncture and chiro should be pre-approved and are not for wellness visits, only for accident, injuries, etc. She understands. She also knows for wellness visits she doesn''t need pre-approval but needs to supply an itemized bill for reimbursement to HAS.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-11 11:45:58', '2024-03-11 11:45:58'),
