  ('zcrm_1579374000134638028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000134663085', 'Alaina Dempsey', NULL, '3-5-24 Alaina came to me via Sara Forrest. Alaina is working for Regis University as a licensed therapist but she''s leaving March 31, 2024 to work on her own independently. Her husband works as an Operations Manager for a moving company. He''s offered ins through them but she''s not offered ins. Their household income is about $125K-$130K for 2024. They won''t qualify for a subsidy. He''s healthy and all set. She has an autoimmune disorder and she needs to take dupixent shots every other week or so. She administers them herself. She''s open to taking the generic form of Dupixent ($3900 on GoodRX!) called Dupilumab 200 mg. Generics show as $35 in the Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0.  She prefers to keep her allergist Dr. Shaila Gogate and will give up her PCP Dr. Kara Burkhardt. Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0 is best at $340.89. She agreed this was the best plan she''s seen when she was looking on her own. She made the 1x payment. She knows to call in two weeks to set up ongoing payments with Cigna. I gave her the phone #. I showed her how to upload her proof of loss of coverage when she gets that from her employer. She seems very capable of completing it on her own when she gets the doc.  She''s all set and very pleased.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-05 12:42:51', '2024-03-05 12:45:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134630055', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012351098', 'Teresa Brachle', NULL, '3/5/24: Emailed Teresa portal credentials and member ID number per yesterdays conversation. I also called and left a voicemail alerting her of the email. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-03-05 12:03:38', '2024-03-05 12:03:38'),
