  ('zcrm_1579374000134588042', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110424026', 'David Waters', NULL, '03.04.2024 Missed David''s call. Called back and LMV. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-03-04 16:33:25', '2024-03-04 16:33:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134588034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129638010', 'Douglas Merrifield', NULL, '03.04.2024 wondering if he has eye coverage. Explained it is not part of the plan unless it is a catastrophe/high medical bill and is affecting the health. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-03-04 16:29:53', '2024-03-04 16:31:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134587286', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082058002', 'Andrea Andersson', NULL, '3-4-24 Andi called right back Now I understand she had reg ins for her husband and herself. But, in order for the kids to have MCS, she has to be on the membership as well. She and kids have been members since Jan. 1st 2022. She got the melanoma removed in Nov. 2022. This is within her time as a member already. So, cancelling her reg ins now shouldn''t be a big risk. The melanoma was super small, one time and no problems since. Her husband is moving onto Medicare soon and Linnea needs her own ins since turning 26.  She will double check the dates and likely cancel their other ins. for her and her husband.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-04 15:45:38', '2024-03-04 15:45:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134587281', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082058002', 'Andrea Andersson', NULL, '3-4-24 Left vm for Andi. She has separate ins she''s been paying for bc of melanoma from 2 years ago. I called to get more details to help her decide if she needs to keep her health ins. still as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-04 15:37:43', '2024-03-04 15:37:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134587276', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178561001', 'Genevieve Choi', NULL, '3-4-24 Genevieve has tried to get the Cobra information from Swedish Medical where William works and they won''t give it to her yet. They are working on an offer to keep him or something along those lines. He''s not going to stay. We''ve set a time for March 18th to potentially enroll Genevieve and some or all kids. Olivia might be best served on Cobra with William. Once they have the numbers they can make an educated decision. He probably will work independently. One place might give him an allowance for medical which would work well for their needs. She will keep me posted. But, they are leaving on Friday for a family vacation until March 17th.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-03-04 15:25:02', '2024-03-04 15:25:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134569048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000133248002', 'Palaniappan Palaniappan', NULL, '3/4/24: Member called needing help with his telehealth. He wanted to link his wife to his account. After I informed him that is not possible, that all members over the age of 18 must have an individual account due to Hippa laws, he got very upset stating that in his 20 years of dealing with companies never in his life has he heard of this, and kept insisting he add his wife as a dependent. I suggested if he had an issue with it, to reach out to Cirrus MD and gave him their customer service email. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-03-04 14:42:51', '2024-03-04 14:42:51'),
