  ('zcrm_1579374000134509003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122122001', 'Elizabeth Bay', 'EMAIL to Concierge Team re: In Network vs. RBP Model', '03.01.2024 I thought I could use my own doctor (attached below is the detailed email with Planstin, Nikita''s, inquiry).
Elizabeth is getting ready to go to a physical on Monday and wants to know how to proceed. The whole purpose and selling point for her to sign up with MPB is that she got to keep her physicians who she''s been using.
I walked her through how to proceed with her preventive appointment, how Planstin does not reimburse, and how to save on RX''s and Lab-work. She will call us back if needs to use more services in her plan.
EMAIL to Concierge Team re: In Network vs. RBP Model
"Greetings MPB team,
I just got off the phone with Nikita from Planstin inquiring about the following:
Does Elizabeth Bay, a mutual member, stay in network (PL) or does her plan allow her to deviate to RBP model, when attending a preventive appointment?
As of June of 2023, when Planstin decided to offer the RBP model to our members, we were coached (I should say I was coached by Cari and Jennifer) to guide members to practice the following:
Use the physician of their choosing for their preventive appointment.
When asked for insurance, present the Planstin card and direct them to call the ----7526 number to bill Planstin.
We further reminded them to connect with us again should they need a prescription filled or get lab work done...amongst other pertinent details for preventive appointment.

The above was offered to all of the members with Planstin in their plans. It was never instructed that some plans can only use RBP and some plans can only use the PHCS network. Therefore, I am a little concerned about how we have been educating our members on their plans and promoting the options at hand, if in fact there are different approaches to using preventive appointments, depending on the plans.

Can you please clarify this? Are there plans that can ONLY use the RBP model, and plan that can only use the PHCS network? 

Thank you so much Joan"                           NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-03-01 12:25:51', '2024-03-01 12:47:18'),
