Sincerely, 

Sedera', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-26 17:08:20', '2024-02-26 17:08:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134197060', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031391042', 'Jonathan VanNoy', NULL, '2-26-24 Nicole and I walked through the Sedera re-enrollment application and selected no for DPC/VPC but yet for MEC and MPB.Health. She needed to check with Jonathan to figure out which bank account to connect with Austin Capital Bank for new Needs. She completed the application successfully. Patti received confirmation from Sedera as well. So, they should be all set. Patti will also change the Advisor to me.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-26 16:40:27', '2024-02-26 16:40:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134196034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129714015', 'Charlene Dickey', NULL, '02.26.2024 Urgent care called on behalf of Charlene wanting to confirm if THEY are in OUR network. I understood what he was asking. I did not correct him on the network part, but I did ask him to have Charlene call us, b/c that is not what I coached her to do.
I decided to call Planstin myself and confirm their preventive services when it came to shingles. Neti, answered and was patient and kind with me, sharing that if Charlene goes to Urgent Care, IT WILL NOT BE COVERED. If Charlene goes to her PCP and makes sure he codes it "PREVENTIVE", then Planstin will cover that. She also mentioned that Charlene can go to a participating pharmacy. If she get prescribed anything, I''ll coach her to do that.
I called Charlene back and repeated the above to her. She was on the phone with her physician and finalizing an appointment. I told her to make sure not to go to the Urgent care, as that would not be covered. She said no I am speaking to my PCP who works at, John Yur (the hospital) (sp?) - 
**************************************************************************************
Did ask if they can code it preventive
NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-26 16:26:43', '2024-02-26 17:23:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134197035', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178561001', 'Genevieve Choi', NULL, '02-26-24 Andrea Hinman sent them to me via Dr. Brent Penman (?). William is a DR himself at Swedish Hospital. He''s ending his employment there on March 31st. They have 4 kids, 3 are out of state for school. They are 24, 22, 21 and 19. Dr. William has cardiac history with an open heart surgery in 2019 and sees a cardiologist 1x per year. They are less concerned about that and more concerned about his 4 meds for diabetes, Repatha 140 mg, Jardiance 25 mg, Rosuvastatin 20 mg and Mounjaro 5 mg. Willing to take generic versions. They get them every 90 days and 4 x year refills. Daughter Olivia has IBS problems and takes Ibsrela but that is super expensive $1700 month. They might press her to take Linzess 145 mg instead. All of these are covered by RMHP but Dr. Christopher Courtney is not in-network. They''d rather change drs. than mess with the medication coverage. Dr. William can accept Cobra if he wants. He''ll talk with his HR person to find out the cost for just him or him and Olivia. Yes, Genevieve did her first mammogram and had never heard of a thermogram. Her daughters do their pap screenings. They are interested in CARE+ $615 and HAS $200 = $815 plus Dr. William and Olivia''s plan. I sent them all scenarios. They are also originally from Canada. They do not qualify for any subsidy since their income is $1M.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-26 16:22:17', '2024-02-26 16:22:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134196029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122567002', 'Alexandra Novo', NULL, '02.26.2024 Alexandra put in an RX request. I sent her the following:

