  ('zcrm_1579374000134162008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130571025', 'Charlotte Cadieux', NULL, '2/26/24: Charlotte called asking how to find a dr to schedule a wellness visit. I showed her how to search the PHCS network and how to present at appt for billing. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-02-26 09:01:03', '2024-02-26 09:01:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134168003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130524012', 'Lisa Parrish', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2024-02-26 08:07:12', '2024-02-26 08:07:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134162003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000127019002', 'Donna Baker', NULL, '2/26/24: Donna called, recently went to the emergency room for a kidney stone and going for a follow up appt today at urologist. She wanted a run down on how to handle this need. I advised to cellect itemized bills from dr office and hospital, and after IUA is met, she can open a sharing request. Trans her over to Zion to set up her member portal. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-02-26 08:02:16', '2024-02-26 08:02:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134143003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000103640002', 'Julie Shaw', NULL, '2/26/24: Responded to Julies email assisting her with logging into the member portal. -WU', 'Willis Upton', 'Willis Upton', '2024-02-26 07:20:12', '2024-02-26 07:20:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134073033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058356696', 'Shawna Rohrbach', NULL, '02.23.2024 Shawna called at 6:55 to ask all about labwork, sharing requests, IUA''s, colonoscopies and ACA guidelines. We spoke till 7:07 and I emailed her resources via CRM. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-23 18:08:51', '2024-02-23 18:08:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134073023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025389081', 'Kelly Mills', NULL, '02.23.2024 Paula, Kelly''s mom called to discuss the matter of Kelly''s plan being cancelled and "no one alerting them of the event". However, when I read the above notes, it dictates that her advisor''s parent advisor made her advisor aware that her membership will be ending due to MCS not being allowed in Washington. 
Paula was taken back since she pays for her daughter''s healthsharing plan, and they did not learn of the cancellation till Kelly went to the doctor very recently. There they shared with her that her plan was cancelled.
I offered Paula Analisa''s number and Wendy''s number to learn of other options that would work for her and Kelly. I also advised Paula to request from Kelly to put her name on the whatever plan they choose, so team members can speak freely to Paula. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-23 17:18:46', '2024-02-23 17:18:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134073018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000125254010', 'Francoise Bunnell', NULL, '02.23.2024 Fran called requesting the 1095 form. I revisited the message Catherine sent via teams regarding the steps to take, when members call and ask for the 1095:
".....Also, here''s some updates on 1095S:
 
Sedera Members (RCI), these will be mailed out by next week. 
Planstin Members, those forms will NOT be available on their portal. If a member calls requesting it, please send their names and email immediately to Patti and Karina. 
Planstin 1095 will be mailed only to the states that has the mandate or those who request it. (you don''t have to mention this over the phone, just get their names and we will mail it to whoever calls). 
 
There''s a compliance reason as of why we are moving forward this way and another reason why we are working on the Planstin Enrollment platform transfer. If you guys have any questions about 1095s please direct those questions to Patti or Karina. 
 
Thank you so much for all the work you do guys ....."

So I offered to collect Fran''s information and send it to the admin team. She said that she''s had issues in receiving emails from us that it always goes to junk, so I let her know that I will mention that to them, and verified her mailing address. It turns out that we had it wrong in the Admin123 platform and she viewed it in her portal, so she used the option in her portal to make the ADDRESS UPDATE.
I will message the admin team to send her the 1095 form. I did offer her the amount to write-off for the "Member & Family" Membership = $110, according to Patti. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-23 16:29:02', '2024-02-23 16:29:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134073013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000086964002', 'Lani Cordova', NULL, '02.23.2024 Lani called to submit a sharing request on behalf of Connon, her son, who broke his right arm. It is not THAT significant, she shared according to the doctor, but wanted to proceed with a sharing request just in case. I explained the deadline and IUA responsibility.
She also mentioned that her provider WILL NOT bill planstin, not call them or anything. I recommended she request a claim form to submit it to Planstin, but she was reluctant as she said isn''t that the same thing. I am NOT 100% on how the claim form request is processed, but I remember two other members and a Planstin rep in the past, proceeded with that process.
I recommended that she speak to Planstin on that subject, since they are the end all be all in making that decision after all.
I transferred her to Zion. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-23 15:49:47', '2024-02-23 15:49:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134072013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065246029', 'Martha Johnson', NULL, '2-23-24 Martha and her husband called to find out if they should be on Essentials or Direct. They have a DPC and she''s a Dr. I let her know Direct is built to be paired with a DPC. She also asked about an HSA compliant option. I let her know there is an option, however they are both retired and have no self-employment income of any kind. So, they don''t qualify. Their friend who is self-employed, told them they can fund an HSA. Now she understands why and that nothing has changed with their membership.  They thanked me and are all set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-23 14:57:32', '2024-02-23 14:57:32'),
