  ('zcrm_1579374000134002041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000076713079', 'Staci Wiley', NULL, '2-22-24 Staci likely qualifies for the FFCRA &amp; ARP but the qualifying questions were asking her about her husbands SE form and she''s not sure. So, she''ll wait for him to answer the rest of the simple questions in the pre-qualifying section. Then she''ll proceed. She knows she will have plenty of time to complete the information for amending her 2021 tax returns. Deadline is April 15th, 2025. She''ll keep me posted.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-22 17:13:18', '2024-02-22 17:13:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134002036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044810847', 'Sally Hammond', NULL, '2-22-24 Sally has an upcoming surgery and things got a bit confusing for her bc she got Redirect involved and Sedera. Sedera has since told her to leave Redirect out of the picture which she will gladly do. She''s been approved for the surgery and up to $20K in sharing. She said the surgery shouldn''t come anywhere near the $20K. The unknown is the anesthesiologist fee.  The hospital is asking for $2500 up front. Intead of completing a long complicated form from Sedera, Sally''s comfortable with putting that on her cc and then including in the Need for reimbursement. Sally will call the hospital one more time to make sure the $2500 is still accurate to go through the surgery process. She now understands the hospital needs to bill her for the remaining costs of the surgery. She will submit those and she has set up the Austin Capital Bank for reimbursements to be shared with her.  She was initially worried about reimbursement taking forever due to her experience with Redirect. Once I understood that, I let her know Sedera hasn''t been a problem with reimbursements in a timely fashion. She''s feeling better about it all and going on a bit of trust. I let her know I''ve had a good experience with my clients with Sedera sharing the cost of their needs. She''s all set for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-22 16:32:58', '2024-02-22 16:32:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134002031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114233002', 'Dilan Bollmann', NULL, '2-22-24 Dilan will update his payment information.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-22 16:14:27', '2024-02-22 16:14:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133971096', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123820012', 'Nancie Hineline', NULL, '02.22.2024 Nancie called to learn how to find an ophthalmologist and if what she is experiencing would be shared. It is revolving around her vision, but not eyewear, sight correction cataract...as far as we know. The CirrusMD physician recommended that she go in to see an Ophthalmologist right away.
Her experience: she noticed flashes of light upper right quadrant of eye
While she was researching it, she started seeing floaters then and the flashes and floaters became more prominent.
She is not experiencing pain or redness.
The CirrusMD physician wrote down: if not able to see an ophthalmologist go to urgent care
She does not wear glasses
Because in the past, Zion concierge has been able to inform whether something might be shareable or not, we did a 3-way call with them, and spoke with Denise. That phone call was not helpful other than Nancie attaining an invitation link to register and open a sharing request to learn whether or not it is shareable.
I sent Nancie the HCBB directions and Healthgrades site to start her search on an Ophthalmologist and make an appointment for tomorrow. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-22 15:27:28', '2024-02-22 15:52:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000134002023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005654211', 'Hans Erickson', NULL, '2-22-24 Hans called to better understand his membership for wellness and Needs. I shared with him the HAS for wellness and he''s very interested.  He plays hockey, skis, has pelaton app for training, etc. He gets his bi-annual dental cleanings and he''s about to do a vision screening and wants an annual wellness visit. So, he may choose to add HAS.
He''s curious about sleep apnea and Nahla read him that part from the Sharing Guidelines that it''s not shared. He''s not eager to go get tested or do any of that from talking with friends. So, we discussed trying alternative, integrative, holistic options instead for a possible different outcome. I let him know alternative must be pre-approved, if there''s a chance it will be shared. He was super appreciative of my help and the fact that I always remember who he is.  He came to me via Matt Ross.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-22 14:43:55', '2024-02-22 14:44:18'),
