  ('zcrm_1579374000133914072', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011521464', 'Jaime Boswell', NULL, '2-21-24 Jaime''s husband is re-employed with benefits beginning March 1. I sent her the cancellation form and cc''ed Patti.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-21 20:54:35', '2024-02-21 20:54:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133914057', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011939106', 'Jessica Muniz', NULL, '2-21-24 Jess thought she might qualify for the FFCRA but when we talked she realized that she was W2 employed at that time. She missed work March 31st-April 12th but had to use her vacation time while working at Holistica. So, she doesn''t qualify for any tax credit.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-21 20:25:19', '2024-02-21 20:25:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133914044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000136382001', 'Eliza Volk', NULL, '2-21-24 Jeremy Colbert referred Eliza Volk to me. Eliza is 36. She watched the MPB video. She''s single, healthy, no meds, no tobacco. She''s self-employed. She wants wellness, gyno, derm, acupuncture, chiro, etc. She just moved to CO from Asheville, NC but she''s originally from NY. She is on her family''s ins plan back in NY for now. She can have the family business end her benefits to create a Life Change Event. She''s guessing $22K but hopeful for $50K. Until she''s surpassing the $22K she may want to choose Cigna Connect CO Option Silver at no cost to her with a $401 APTC and cost of the plan is $396.92. DOB 9-12-87 and zip 80304.  She''s also interested in counseling as a benefit.  She''s thinking of doing Cigna at no cost and HAS for the wellness benefits that are far more aligned with her desires and the mental health benefit.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-21 20:17:37', '2024-02-21 20:20:46'),
