  ('zcrm_1579374000133697018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000133855019', 'Talya Dash', NULL, '2-19-24 Talya is 42 and super healthy, no meds, no tobacco, no drugs, no alcohol. She''s self-employed but never sees a Dr. She doesn''t do the traditional annual wellness screenings. She prefers naturopathic, holistic alternatives, including acupuncture, chiro, supplements, etc. She''s not interested in MEC but possibly in HAS. She has her own S-Corp. Their household income is about $200-$220K as her best guess for 2024. They don''t qualify for a subsidy. The cheapest ACA plan starts at $307 and the Cigna $0 Ded Bronze plan is $403 with a $9450 MOP.  She''s interested in CARE+ $1000 at $265 and possibly HAS $107 for total of $372.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-19 11:00:25', '2024-02-19 11:00:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133723008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071028001', 'Randy Morgan', NULL, '02.19.2024 Randy called a bit frustrated regarding the email sent out on the new Planstin cards. He got the impression, he does not get to use his plan on anything and just present as a "self-pay" patient. He was concerned should he end up in the ER room that he will need to pay for everything, so what was the point of him getting this plan.
