  ('zcrm_1579374000133513033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130295012', 'Aana Camp', NULL, '02.15.2024 Aana has knees issues and needs to see an Orthopedic, who she has one in mind. I offered her guidance and directions on HCBB and Healthgrades, via Outlook. Aana was able to log into HCBB while we were on the phone together. I explained all that she can benefit from the site: fair pricing and quality care on searches for Physicians, Facilities and Procedures and Hospitals. I explained that her having issues in both knees, will result in separate IUA''s if the time comes to that. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-15 17:57:07', '2024-02-15 18:06:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133513028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000068391103', 'Diana Freeman', NULL, '02.15.2024 Diana called on behalf of her daughter needing to get a test for up and coming nurses called, Titer~.
I guided her to use HCBB, healthgrades.com to find a PCP as a lead step and discussed how this would be a  cash-pay visit, and she could dip into the HSA account to pay, since it is not a preventive nor a large medical bill. 
I also sent her directions to have on how to search HCBB and the healthgrades link. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-15 17:46:26', '2024-02-15 17:46:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133553008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000133552021', 'Scott Filion', NULL, '2-15-24 Scott lives in Louisville and was referred by Pam Buderus. Scott is 53, his partner is 54 and his kids are 23, 21 and 18. He''s considering retiring ongoing. He left his job in Sept. 2023. He''s on Cobra now for $1700 a month which allows out of network benefits for his kids who are in Portland, OR, Notre Dame and one is in Boulder. His wife passed away 2 1/2 years ago! He files taxes as widowed w/ dependents. So, he can''t include his partner on ACA. But, with CARE+ he could include her since they live together. CARE+ is best since retired. Scott has a cardiac thing related to covid just about 2 years ago.  His cardiologist says please don''t come back since he''s super healthy. However, he seems to possibly want to do a nuclear med scan to make 100% certain he''s all set. He says that costs a ton. Perhaps he''ll do that while he has his Cobra. He''s in no rush to do it. He also takes a statin purely bc his father had high cholesterol. He doesn''t but he''s taking it to be safe.  His son had his spleen taken out about 2 years ago as well. He understands the pre-x clause and will wait until all of these things are far enough in the past to avoid the pre-x clause.  His daughter had an eating disorder when her mom passed. But, she''s good now and no meds.  He knows CirrusMD bc he was asked to be on the board a while back. He declined but he knows one of the board members well. Small world.  I quoted CARE+ $875/$1000 and $125/$25. Also interested in HAS, $250. He will find out the dates of the health items above. He''s thinking if he moves forward it will be summer or fall, mostly likely to play it safe.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-15 17:34:37', '2024-02-15 17:48:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133553003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000134180005', 'Lisa Ben-Zeev', NULL, '2-15-24 Referred by Beth Blacker. Lisa just quit her job on Feb. 1st. She''s not sure if she has ins. in Feb. She was assuming so, but she was refunded her $200 for her payment towards her ins. I assume she doesn''t have coverage. They never gave her a Cobra notice either. So, she will inquire about that. She doens''t have any pre-x. She only had a minute to talk. So, I sent her the video to watch in case that resonates with her. Otherwise, we''ll explore ACA. She needs something March 1st for sure.  We will talk on Monday.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-15 17:31:31', '2024-02-26 11:55:34'),
