  ('zcrm_1579374000133350078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110308002', 'Robert Golden', NULL, '2/13/24: Robert called asking about new Planstin card and if he can expect a physical one. Called planstin and they said....no, physical cards are not being mailed out.
He also wanted to know why there are copays listed on the card. I advised that it doesn''t really apply to him, but according to Planstin - copays are now listed on the HSA MEC cards with the deductible, and do in fact go into effect if a member ever has an accumulation of office visits that are billed to planstin and reach the deductible. 
I asked P to mail Robert a physical card. Followed up with him via email. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-02-13 14:02:15', '2024-02-13 14:02:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133350073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060480020', 'Marian Salley', 'RCVD MPowering Benefits Existing Member Change Form 02.13.2024', '02.13.2024 Marian''s bday in our system is wrong. I sent her the MPowering Benefits Existing Member Change Form and she sent it in TODAY to change the year on there. She will call back on Thursday to confirm the update. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-13 13:43:07', '2024-02-13 13:43:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133350068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000093632002', 'Adrian Piazza', NULL, '02.13.2024 MPowering Benefits Existing Member Change Form was sent to Corinne to remove both daughters. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-13 13:31:25', '2024-02-13 13:31:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133343216', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078309004', 'James Skurski', NULL, '2-13-24 James called to cancel bc his wife didn''t know all of the benefits included in the membership and felt like it was only for catastrophic needs. I spent about 40 minutes explaining all that is included in the membership. She paid cash for her mammo back in Nov. since they didn''t have a Planstin card. She needs to get her blood checked 2x per year and Dr. forces a Dr. visit every 3 months for her thyroid meds which she''s annoyed about. She will try CirrusMD. I gave her a link to get her labs at the best price. I quoted her the Co-Pay plan for almost $1000 a month since she wanted co-pays. But, they can get ACA for $475 which they joined in Jan. After talking with her and helping her understand how to use her membership she may cancel ACA. Jim might need  a hip surgery in the next year or two. They are in their 3rd year of membership so they get up to $50K for pre-x and up to $125K after Nov. 2024. They will call the MPB Concierge Team to ask for help with highest quality care for best price in their local area. She will work on that next. She has CirrusMD and now she knows how to get her labs super affordably. She was super appreciative of my knowledge.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-13 13:22:47', '2024-02-13 13:22:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133350058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064054002', 'Mark Dunkley', 'SENT the Permission Form to  Speak to the MPB Plan 02.13.2024', '02.13.2024 Wife called needing to take Mark to the ER and wanted to know what to do. I guided her to go straight to either the ER or urgent care and present as a cash pay patient and collect all the receipts.
Then I sent Mark the Permission to Discuss the MPB.Health Membership Plan to complete and add her. I did not catch her name, but will add it when we receive the form. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-13 12:57:00', '2024-02-13 12:57:00'),
