Child 8-7-2018', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2024-02-12 14:50:35', '2024-02-12 15:13:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133299040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027924354', 'Darrin Hallman', NULL, '2-12-24 Darrin talked with Angee to get his 1095-C tax form and Zion came up. He''s friends with their CEO Brett Saunders (I think he said?) who is in his rotary club. He thought it might be good to switch. However, it won''t help him bc the membership contribution is more and he has a heart pre-x which precludes him from moving. So, he will gladly stay put with PSDHC and Sedera. He thinks he costly to Sedera as it is. Very nice guy. He lives in St. George, UT. He''s paying $892/$1000 IUA and witH SECURE HSA it''s $1005/$1000.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-12 14:49:57', '2024-02-12 14:50:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133290013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000131174002', 'Shane de Garay', NULL, '2/12/24: Cristi called in and mentioned that one of their daughters had been bit by a dog that required two stitches and wanted to know how to submit a sharing request. Had additional questions about subrogation due to it being the dog owners'' fault, directed her to reach out to zion health for this particular inquiry. -WU', 'Willis Upton', 'Willis Upton', '2024-02-12 14:49:03', '2024-02-12 14:49:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133275088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027924354', 'Darrin Hallman', NULL, '2/12/24: Darrin called to check on 1095. Since he is Sedera, I advised they will be sent out in the next couple of weeks. During our conversation, Zion was mentioned. He was intrigued that we worked with Zion bc they are local to him, and asked what it would look like if he were to switch his plan over to them. I advised he speak with his advisor, Wendy. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-02-12 14:40:50', '2024-02-12 14:40:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133299032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109620011', 'Monique Koen', NULL, '2-12-24 Monique got a new job with benefits for March 1st, I believe. I sent her the cancellation form. I also let her know it''s best to keep the HMA active until she uses up the funds in it.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-12 14:36:10', '2024-02-12 14:36:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133299024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000133641002', 'Darrell Creekmore', NULL, '2-12-24 Darrel is 40 and his wife is 37. Anu Lawrence referred them to me. He''s a healthcare provider himself. His wife is a dental hygienist. She was getting benefits but is now working as a dental hygienist for the secret service (?? I think that''s what he said!)  She''s only working part-time now, so she no longer gets benefits. Their insurance ended Jan. 31st. They were paying only about $300 he thinks. He couldn''t remember. They are mostly healthy, no tobacco, no drugs, no obesity, etc. His wife has sports induced asthma and just uses an inhaler before athletics. She also has a benign, non-cancerous tumor on the pituitary gland that has No growth in 5 years. She takes a half dose of medication for every two weeks to manage it. It''s inconsequential according to Darrel. Medication is super affordable paying with cash. I think he said the medical term is prolactinoma. Per his work, he seemed very knowledgeable explaining it to me. I explained the pre-x clause in depth  and he''s not concerned. He''s most interested in the CARE+ $2500 / $360 since they really don''t use the system very much. He doesn''t want the extra expenses of wellness. He wants to run it by his wife and then he''s ready to enroll tonight or tomorrow morning.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-12 13:01:02', '2024-02-16 11:11:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133296024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129963009', 'Zachary Krapfl', NULL, '02.12.2024 Robyn put in an RX request for:Olmesartan Medoxomil: QTY 30 • 40 MG • Tablet 
I sent her the following:
We were able to find you a coupon for:
Olmesartan Medoxomil: QTY 30 • 40 MG • Tablet 
The prices below are as of today 02.12.2024:
Olmesartan Medoxomil: QTY 30 • 40 MG • Tablet: City Market = $10.75
Please let us know if you need anything changed or adjusted.
We are here at the concierge line M-F from 9am - 8pm EST.                                          NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-02-12 12:48:05', '2024-02-12 12:48:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133296019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014539007', 'Kris Srnka', 'Rcv''d Cancellation Form - Processed - #3054', '02.12.2024 Kris called b/c she received an EOB bill for $864, even though she has cancelled with MPB due to aging out into medicare. Kris and I did a three way call to Planstin, where the EOB came from, and Nikita shared that she is not showing up that she is cancelled on their end, which means that the integration file issues are at it with cancelling members as well. 
I messaged Patti via teams to ask her, even though CRM and Admin123 show that Kris is cancelled, to offer any insight she might see on her end.
