  ('zcrm_1579374000133232018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096344002', 'Mark Leubscher', NULL, '02.09.24:  Recv. an email from Wendy. Denny Watkins emailed her asking her to have someone from the MPB Concierge Team call Mark Leubscher and try to help him with the following issue:

From: Sabrina Leubscher <sabrinaleubscher@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, Feb 8, 2024 at 1:15 PM
Subject: Medical bills unpaid
To: Dennis Watkins <tmwinsuranceagency@gmail.com>
Cc: Mark Leubscher Leubscher <mark.leubscher@yahoo.com>

Good Afternoon, 

I have bills from Quest diagnostics that have gone unpaid and are now in collections against me. These bills are from my annual blood work completed by Doctor Neil A Patterson''s Office. There are 4 separate bills ($29.41, $654.00, $267.88, $148.10) totaling the amount of $1099.39. The first 3 are all from the same days blood work completed on 05/19/23. The last one ($148.10) is from annual blood work completed back on 10/04/22 also at Neil A Patterson''s Office. I am not sure why they are different amounts as they were both annual blood draws that were completed at Patterson''s Office and sent to Quest.

I know when I spoke with you last year regarding a discrepancy in charges by Patterson’s Office for our annual blood work, it was explained to me that there is a negotiated contract rate between your company and Quest for a specific amount. I will either be charged that one time amount by either Quest or my doctors office. Why I was charged by Quest for different amounts for the same blood work that was all routine and why none of it has been paid by your company I don’t understand. How can we get this issue resolved as soon as possible as this is now affecting my credit?  

I have attached the bills from Quest as well as the collection accounts that I have now been charged for your reference. 

Thank You, 
Sabrina Leubscher

Emailed Sabrina the explanation of payment Dr. Paterson''s administrator, Julia explained to Denny and Denny subsequently explained to Mark and Sabrina (see notes below). Suggested she contact Dr. Paterson''s office and speak with either Dr. Paterson or his administrator about the double pmt. issue. I offered to discuss it further with her if she needed more clarity and, although she has to deal directly with Dr. Patterson''s office about medical issues, I offered to support her in any way I can..  I asked her to let me know how she wants to move forward.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2024-02-09 13:45:50', '2024-02-09 14:45:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000133234003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000133214002', 'Robert Grinnell', NULL, '2-9-24 Chad enrolled in CARE+ since they don''t think they''ll use the HSA for tax benefits. They will use the wellness benefits and are choosing HAB when available. Total will be $635 CARE+ and $250 = $885.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-02-09 13:43:41', '2024-02-09 13:43:41'),
