  ('zcrm_1579374000132398003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104032', 'Clove Berger', NULL, '1-26-24 Clove called needing to use CirrusMD but somebody told her she has Teladoc. She must have called Planstin or Zion. I gave her the Concierge # as well in case she can''t login. She will do that right away.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-26 16:51:28', '2024-01-26 16:51:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000132389043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129753002', 'Christopher Rape', NULL, '01.26.2024: Pamela put in an rx request on the 25th. 
I sent her the following:
I am glad to have found you some savings.
Attached are 3 coupons that match the strength/dosage requested for:
Synthroid: 125mg - 90 Tablets
Junel Fe: 1.5-30 - 90 Days
USUALLY, Junel 1.5/30 (and its branded generics) comes in a 21-day pack. Each tablet contains 1.5 mg norethindrone acetate and 30 mcg ethinyl estradiol.
The typical dose is to take 1 tablet by mouth daily for 21 days, followed by 7 days off (not taking any tablets). So you will find for your 90 day request, I included a 63 tablet coupon (21 tablets/pack), and 84 tablet coupon (28 tablets/pack, which seems to give you an extra month if one is supposed to take a break for 7 days).

The prices attached are as of today, 01.26.2024:
Publix
Synthroid: 125mg - 90 Tablets = $142.95
Junel Fe: 1.5-30 - 90 Days = $18.71 for 84 Tablets and $16.50 for 63 Tablets
I reached out to our international shopper to find a better deal on Synthroid-BRAND, and he responded to me with the following quote. If you''re interested in proceeding with this route, please feel free to reach out to him with the information included below.
QUOTE: Synthroid 125mcg x 90tabs $75.95 + $9.95 shipping...................................NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-01-26 16:44:37', '2024-01-26 16:44:37'),
