  ('zcrm_1579374000132261168', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001637239', 'Dean Dealy', NULL, '1-25-24 Dean''s policy is issued successfully. I called Mara to verify that we built it properly. We built it to maximize his ability to fund it more than $500 a month.  If he doens''t do so in the first 1-2 years then we will want to shrink the policy down modestly so it doesn''t elapse after about 20 years. Assuming he''s able to fund it more than $500 at times, then this will allow him the most flexibility in his policy to expand it as he continues to earn more and feels confident in his ability to fund it. Per the illustration, the policy will lapse in years 21-40 unless he funds it more. So, I just spoke with him and we will revisit this next year around his DOB of Jan. 5th to review it. If he hasn''t funded it with any additional funds all year then we will shrink the policy without penalty. We structured it so he can fund it more and not have to get a new policy as he becomes more financially well. Again, we can shrink it if he feels uncomfortable next year.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-01-25 15:56:18', '2024-01-25 15:56:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000132312062', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115183002', 'Thomas Leach', NULL, '01.25.2024 Thomas called unfortunately with an injured finger from two months ago.
He needed to know who to go see and how to get covered.
I explained the process for cash pay visits and why this is out of pocket and not "covered". He was surprised to learn that he does not have insurance for accidents.
I offered to search for physicians in his area via HCBB and send it to him. I did and sent him the instructions and links to freely search HCBB and healthgrades. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-01-25 15:50:25', '2024-01-25 16:18:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000132346056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000072425023', 'Lior Moshe', NULL, '1/25/24: 
Adria was misinformed about how to use plan back in the summer (so she says). 
She presented incorrectly and paid for her wellness visit. 
We spoke to Planstin together and Nakita advised her to send the bill to the claims department for reimbursement to the provider - then the provider could pay the overage to her. 

*** Sent a very detailed email on 1/26/24 with written instructions about how and why she should present depending on whether she is using MEC and Zion cost sharing. ****

Aside from solving the issue at hand,
Adria insisted on ranting  ~on and on and on and on and on and on~  about how it is the Concierge''s fault that this has happened because one person tells her everything is cash pay, and someone else tells her something different, and all she did was follow directions. From the notes above, it looks like she''s been educated multiple times by MPB members that wouldn''t mislead her. She is downright hateful to the Concierge team and I''m not sure if any amount of education will "fix" the situation in her head.

To wrap up her rant, I asked "What then, would you like us to do to right this situation?" She replied with, "I want specific instructions in writing so I can clearly understand what to say to providers."
See email titled "Using your MEC &  Health Sharing Services."
 
AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-01-25 15:27:10', '2024-01-26 14:52:40'),
