  ('zcrm_1579374000132261075', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001637239', 'Dean Dealy', NULL, '1-19-24 Dean and I have been discussing life ins policy options for at least 5 years. He''s finally ready to take the plunge and work towards protecting himself and creating a path towards retirement income. He''s a life long cyclists and used to be a high level competitor. He now cycles for fun. He never goes to the doctors unless he has any accidents from cycling. He''s never had a PCP until now. He decided to test out a new Dr. today to get a baseline for his health with labs, etc. 
Mara helped me illustrate a NLG  Flexlife IUL for $75 Face Amount and $200K additional death benefit to be funded $500 a month. Minimum premium is $2,002.92 annually. Max funding amount is $21,088 per year to avoid MEC.  Run at Standard Non-Tobacco. DOB 1-5-1971.
We completed his application in person.  He used to take Prozac for depression but quit less than a year ago. The application is complete and awaiting a response. His dad died around age 65 from cancer and his mom is still alive and well. Income and assets is around $143K. 
